# Create a Linux or Windows Self-Hosted Agent in Azure DevOps

---

## ✅ What is a Self-Hosted Agent?

A **self-hosted agent** is an agent that you install and run on your own machines (Linux or Windows) to execute Azure DevOps pipeline jobs instead of using Microsoft-hosted agents.

---

## ✅ Steps to Create a Self-Hosted Agent

### 1. Navigate to Agent Pools

- Go to **Project Settings > Agent Pools**.
- Use the default pool or create a new one.

---

### 2. Download and Configure the Agent

#### 🐧 For Linux:

```bash
# Download the agent package
wget https://vstsagentpackage.azureedge.net/agent/3.225.0/vsts-agent-linux-x64-3.225.0.tar.gz

# Extract it
tar zxvf vsts-agent-linux-x64-3.225.0.tar.gz

# Navigate into the extracted folder
cd myagent

# Configure the agent
./config.sh --url https://dev.azure.com/YOUR_ORG \
            --auth pat \
            --token YOUR_PAT \
            --pool default \
            --agent self-hosted-agent

# Install and start the service
sudo ./svc.sh install
sudo ./svc.sh start
